  "stem": "What is the sum of all solutions to the equation \\(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x + 2} = \\frac{3}{4}\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "2/3"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Multiply both sides by \\(4x(x + 2)\\): \\(4(x + 2) + 4x = 3x(x + 2)\\), so \\(8x + 8 = 3x^{2} + 6x\\).",
    "Rearrange: \\(3x^{2} - 2x - 8 = 0\\), so \\((3x + 4)(x - 2) = 0\\) and \\(x = 2\\) or \\(x = -\\frac{4}{3}\\).",
    "Neither value makes a denominator zero, so both are solutions. The sum is \\(2 - \\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nsols = solve(Eq(1/x + 1/(x + 2), Rational(3, 4)), x)\nassert set(sols) == {2, Rational(-4, 3)}\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == sum(sols)",
